# systemd-tmpfiles rule for hsm-linux-probe, installed as /usr/lib/tmpfiles.d/hsm-linux-probe.conf
# by packaging/build-deb.sh.
#
# The probe rolls its log file daily (hsm-linux-probe_<UTC date>.log in the unit's LogsDirectory=)
# but never deletes one. systemd-tmpfiles-clean.timer (daily) removes files in that directory that
# were last written more than 30 days ago; today's file is written continuously and never is.
# "m:" ages by the modification time only, so an operator reading an old log (atime) does not keep
# it alive (the age-by prefix needs systemd >= 250; Debian 13 ships 257). "e" only ages the
# contents of an existing directory: it neither creates it nor changes its owner or mode, which
# stay LogsDirectory='s (hsm-probe, 0750). The same lines also go to the journal, whose retention
# is the host's journald configuration.
e /var/log/hsm-linux-probe - - - m:30d
